  "description": "Learn how to navigate stores, ask for prices, and pay for items in German.",
  "guidebook": "Welcome to shopping in German! Asking about prices is simple: use **Wie viel kostet...?** for a single item (*Wie viel kostet das Brot?*) and **Wie viel kosten...?** for plurals (*Wie viel kosten die Äpfel?*).\n\nWhen you reach the register (**die Kasse**), cashiers frequently ask: **\"Bar oder mit Karte?\"** (Cash or card?). Cash is still very popular in Germany, especially at local bakeries and open-air markets (**der Markt**).\n\n*Helpful tip:* Most supermarkets charge for shopping bags (**die Tasche**), so locals almost always bring their own reusable bags! Also, note that most retail stores in Germany remain closed on Sundays.",
